========== 第7章: newaliases は sendmail 互換の別名（postfix では postalias を走らせる） ==========

$ ls -l /usr/bin/newaliases /usr/bin/mailq
lrwxrwxrwx 1 root root 16 May  6 00:47 /usr/bin/mailq -> ../sbin/sendmail
lrwxrwxrwx 1 root root 16 May  6 00:47 /usr/bin/newaliases -> ../sbin/sendmail

$ man 1 sendmail 2>/dev/null | grep -A1 -E '^ +-bi '
       -bi    Initialize alias database. See the newaliases command above.


$ man 1 sendmail 2>/dev/null | sed -n '/^DESCRIPTION/,$p' | grep -A7 -E '^ +newaliases$'
       newaliases
              Initialize  the  alias  database.  If no input file is specified
              (with the -oA option, see  below),  the  program  processes  the
              file(s)  specified with the alias_database configuration parame‐
              ter.  If no alias database type is specified, the  program  uses
              the  type specified with the default_database_type configuration
              parameter.  This mode of operation is implemented by running the
              postalias(1) command.


========== 第7章: .forward は group だけ書ける 664 なら読まれ、other も書ける 666 なら読まれない ==========

$ echo 'alice: bob' >> /etc/aliases

$ newaliases

$ printf 'root\n' > /home/bob/.forward

$ chown bob:bob /home/bob/.forward

$ chmod 664 /home/bob/.forward

$ ls -l /home/bob/.forward
-rw-rw-r-- 1 bob bob 5 Oct 13 11:43 /home/bob/.forward

$ echo "664 で送る" | mail -s "group-writable" alice

$ grep -c "664 で送る" /var/mail/root
1

$ chmod 666 /home/bob/.forward

$ ls -l /home/bob/.forward
-rw-rw-rw- 1 bob bob 5 Oct 13 11:43 /home/bob/.forward

$ echo "666 で送る" | mail -s "world-writable" alice

$ grep -c "666 で送る" /var/mail/root /var/mail/bob
/var/mail/root:0
/var/mail/bob:1

$ grep -h "world writable" /var/log/mail.log /var/log/syslog
2026-10-13T02:43:35.785172+00:00 linuc postfix/local[600]: warning: file /home/bob/.forward is world writable
2026-10-13T02:43:35.785172+00:00 linuc postfix/local[600]: warning: file /home/bob/.forward is world writable


========== 第5章: /var/log/journal が無い環境での永続化（最後に打つ。journal を消すため） ==========

$ rm -rf /var/log/journal

$ systemctl restart systemd-journald

$ ls -d /var/log/journal/* /run/log/journal/* 2>&1
ls: cannot access '/var/log/journal/*': No such file or directory
/run/log/journal/f5295b64ae1a49b9a1af1c892764514b

$ mkdir -p /var/log/journal

$ systemd-tmpfiles --create --prefix /var/log/journal

$ journalctl --flush

$ ls -d /var/log/journal/* /run/log/journal/* 2>&1
ls: cannot access '/var/log/journal/*': No such file or directory
/run/log/journal/f5295b64ae1a49b9a1af1c892764514b

$ systemctl restart systemd-journald

$ ls -d /var/log/journal/* /run/log/journal/* 2>&1
ls: cannot access '/run/log/journal/*': No such file or directory
/var/log/journal/f5295b64ae1a49b9a1af1c892764514b

$ journalctl -t systemd-journald --no-pager | grep -E "(System|Runtime) Journal" | tail -2
Oct 13 11:43:38 linuc systemd-journald[622]: Runtime Journal (/run/log/journal/f5295b64ae1a49b9a1af1c892764514b) is 8.0M, max 1.8G, 1.8G free.
Oct 13 11:43:40 linuc systemd-journald[639]: System Journal (/var/log/journal/f5295b64ae1a49b9a1af1c892764514b) is 8.0M, max 4.0G, 3.9G free.
